<title>UK: NWE jet fuel premiums stable.</title>
<headline>NWE jet fuel premiums stable.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE jet fuel prices slid in line with benchmark futures on Tuesday but premiums were steady in quiet business, traders said.</p>
<p>Benchmark Dec IPE futures declined $1.25 to $217.75 a tonne on heavy selling by a broking house.</p>
<p>Steady demand for larger parcels and lack of availability of sizeable cargoes continued to support cargo premiums, which were around Dec IPE +$33/34 cif NWE. Barges were around Dec IPE +$28.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
